note OVITO 3.17.2 reads extended XYZ periodicity and an out-of-cell second frame without wrapping or repeating frame 0.
note A timed write is rejected unless its file is non-empty, inside that format's size range, and reads back at the full atom count. That check runs after the clock stops.
note Every write sample except the 1M readcon-con row is the interleaved fresh-process measurement from this session. The clock is serialise and store of a structure that already exists: see each row's Clock note. The 1M readcon-con write is the back-to-back serial measurement, 0.1701 s. Default threads are 0.0577 s. Chemfiles has no CON writer, so its write cell is 'no writer'.
