warm reads the file once before the clock; cold drops the page cache after warmup
every timed read copies positions and the cell into numpy and checks the sum
frames 1M n_frames 1 unique 1
note chemfiles has no native CON format; the chemfiles-con row copies positions and the cell out of a chemfiles Frame filled from readcon.
note chemfiles compression library (bundled) opens {"bz2": true, "gz": true, "trr": true, "xz": true}
note mda-h5md omitted; MDAnalysis 2.11.0 H5MDReader needs h5py, which is not installed.
note mda-mmcif omitted; MDAnalysis 2.11.0 MMCIFReader needs gemmi, which is not installed.
note MDAnalysis 2.11.0 on DCD, XTC, NetCDF, TRR, XYZ, PDB, H5MD and mmCIF where those readers import. Cells are orthogonal, so the 2.11 triclinic wrap does not apply.
note extxyz-ng 0.0.2 was not added. Installing that wheel on the default path replaces the extxyz 0.4.6 module (same import name, no read_dicts). extxyz 0.4.6 stays. The side prefix build/bench/extxyz-ng-0.0.2 was not present, so there is no read arm. bench/h2h/install_extxyz_ng.sh installs the hashed wheel there.
note mdcompress 1.0.0 is not on PyPI. The refresh-bio binary and its in-memory reader were not both available, so the row is omitted.
note 1M readcon-chemfiles round-trip position 0.05 cell 0 exceeds 0.0001
note 1M chemfiles-xyz round-trip position 0.05 cell 0 exceeds 0.0001
unsupported 1M mda-pdb unsupported: PDB atom serial is five digits (max 99999 atoms)
note 1M readcon-con serial fresh-process read 0.0964 s, default threads 0.0917 s. The table row is the interleaved serial measurement. Default threads is one worker per core, same warmup and sample count (12).
